## 1. Review & Understand

**Objective**
- Explain *why* `POST /api/files/diff` can still be sent several times in a short window.
- Make the cache work at the **transport level**, so any POST (not only the one wrapped by `files.diff`) is cached/served by a **hash of its body**.

**Findings (root causes, in order of impact)**

| # | Cause | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **The cache is opt-in per module.** Only `files.diff`/`files.read` go through `API.cached()`. Any other `API.post('/api/files/diff', ...)` (or a future caller) bypasses it completely and hits the backend. | `src/api/modules/files.js` vs `src/api/api.js` |
| 2 | **The in-flight key keeps the raw body.** `_requestKey()` uses `JSON.stringify(data)`, so the key for a diff contains the entire file content — `JSON.stringify` runs on *every* call and a ~1 MB string lives in the Map until settle. It is not a *hash*. | `_requestKey` in `src/api/api.js` |
| 3 | **Path variants break both cache hits and invalidation.** `FileViewer` calls `files.read('./' + filePath)`, `PRFile`/`PRViewer` call `files.read(fileFullName)` (absolute), `CodeViewer` calls `files.diff({ path: this.file })`. `./src/a.js` and `src/a.js` are two different keys → two backend reads, and `write('src/a.js')` does **not** invalidate the `./src/a.js` entry (stale hit). | `FileViewer.vue`, `PRFile.vue`, `CodeViewer.vue` |
| 4 | **Non-serializable bodies are wrongly deduped.** `JSON.stringify(new FormData())` → `"{}"`, so two concurrent `upload`/`uploadMultiple` calls share **one** request and the second file is silently lost. | `files.upload`, `files.uploadMultiple`, `images.upload`, `tools.imageToText` |
| 5 | Calls with **different content** (streaming/edited code blocks) legitimately produce different keys — those can never be merged; that is caller-side behaviour, not a cache defect. | `CodeViewer.loadDiffInfo()` |

## 2. Change Proposal

1. **`requestCache.js`** — add the key primitives the transport layer needs:
   - `serializeBody(data)` → stable string, or `null` when the body must not be cached (`FormData`/`Blob`/`ArrayBuffer`).
   - `hashBody(data)` → short hash of the serialized body (this is the "POST hashed" part).
   - `normalizePath(value)` → `./a/b.js`, `a/b.js`, `a//b.js` collapse into one key (fixes hits + invalidation).
2. **`api.js`** — new `API.request(method, url, data, { key, ttl, force })`:
   - always runs through `_dedupedRequest` (concurrent identical calls wait for the running promise);
   - when `ttl` is given it additionally runs through `RequestCache.run()` (short-term reuse);
   - the default key is `METHOD:preparedUrl:hash(body)` — **no body in memory, POST included**;
   - non-serializable bodies get a unique key → never deduped/cached.
   `get/del/post/put/delete` become thin wrappers accepting an optional `options` argument (backwards compatible).
3. **`modules/files.js`** — `read()`/`diff()` declare their cache at the transport call (`API.get(url, { key, ttl, force })`), and every mutation invalidates by **normalized path segment** so all path variants die together.

Risks: cached values are shared by reference (read-only, already documented); explicit `key` must stay project+path qualified (guaranteed by `fileKey()`).

## 3. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/api/requestCache.js` | `serializeBody`, `hashBody`, `normalizePath`; docs updated. |
| `src/api/api.js` | `API.request()` transport-level cache/dedupe; hashed keys; safe handling of `FormData`; `get/post/put/del/delete` accept `options`. |
| `src/api/modules/files.js` | `fileKey()` + path normalization; `read`/`diff` cached at transport level; invalidation by normalized segment. |

## 4. The Changes

